  "rationale": "No single blocked step cuts off the target, because the target is an OR node with several independent ways in. (1) Through appServer:lateralMovement to codeRepo, vaultRead or dbReplica. appServer itself is an OR node with three reachable parents: memoryDump (from wifiGuest, supplychain or exposedApi), apiToken (browserStore AND iotDevice, both reachable) and ssoLogin (configSecret AND dmzWeb, both reachable). (2) Through jumpHost:lateralMovement to shareMount, which does not use appServer at all. jumpHost is an OR node reachable from configSecret (from supplychain) or from dbLogin (ciRunner AND sshKey, both reachable). Blocking appServer leaves jumpHost to shareMount to target. Blocking jumpHost leaves appServer to codeRepo or vaultRead to target. Every other non-target step lies on at most one of several redundant routes, so blocking it alone leaves the target reachable."
